A new optional `agents` extra: `langchain`, `langgraph`, `langchain-ollama`, `langchain-openai`, `langchain-anthropic`, `langgraph-checkpoint-postgres` and `langchain-mcp-adapters`. Optional for the reason `mcp` is: `models.py` imports none of it, so a deployment that only catalogs models installs none of it. `services/agents.py` imports one provider package, lazily, chosen by the recorded dialect of the provider.

The extra deliberately does **not** carry psycopg 3, although `langgraph-checkpoint-postgres` needs it. Django prefers psycopg 3 over psycopg2 whenever it can import it, so installing it changes the database driver of the whole deployment; under that driver Nautobot's change logging was measured to deadlock, because the JSON adapter iterates a queryset on a cursor that is already mid-statement. An optional extra of one app must not do that to a deployment. A deployment that wants a Postgres checkpointer installs psycopg 3 itself, having read the warning on the AI Agent Thread page. Nothing in this app needs it: the retention functions use Django's own connection.

`langgraph-checkpoint-postgres` moved out of the `agents` extra into a `checkpointer` extra of its own, and out of `all`. It hard-depends on psycopg 3, and pip resolves that transitively, so leaving the package in `agents` installed psycopg 3 anyway — the exact thing the previous note said it avoided. Django prefers psycopg 3 over psycopg2 whenever it can import it, which changes the database driver of the whole deployment; under that driver Nautobot's change logging deadlocks. Nothing in this app needs the package: retention runs on Django's own connection.
